Hi,

we're running Dunix 4.0D. I have a question re syslog, we have setup
syslog.conf to log the normal way:

kern.debug              /var/adm/syslog.dated/kern.log
user.debug              /var/adm/syslog.dated/user.log
mail.debug              /var/adm/syslog.dated/mail.log
daemon.debug            /var/adm/syslog.dated/daemon.log
auth.debug              /var/adm/syslog.dated/auth.log
syslog.debug            /var/adm/syslog.dated/syslog.log
lpr.debug               /var/adm/syslog.dated/lpr.log

msgbuf.err              /var/adm/crash/msgbuf.savecore

kern.debug              /var/adm/messages
kern.debug              /dev/console
*.emerg                 *

Then this is sent to a central node:

*.emerg;*.alert;*.crit;*.err;*.warning;*.notice;*.info;mail.none
@1xx.xx.xxx.34
kern.debug;mail.crit;mail.err           @1xx.xx.xxx.34


When we want to test this, is it possible to use logger to write to
kern.log?

For example this writes to daemon.log, and to the remote node
logger -p daemon.crit "testing"

But this writes to user.log, and not to the remote node
logger -p kern.crit "testing again"

Thanks,

