We had problems to write from our Alpha onto a NFS mounted disk on a Sun Sol.5.6
for a couple of days. The KEY to solve this problem is to switch to NFS
VERSION 2 ! Just add -nfsv2 to the mount - options in /etc/fstab or
/etc/auto_master (if using automount). The performance increases by a factor
of 100 ! Suns and DEC's V3 implementations seem to be different.
