> Is there someone, who has a tool, which make it possible
> to skip after the eot mark of the DAT tape and read the
> corrupted tar archive ?
>
> Kai
>
>

We are one of the companies that recovers data from this situation. The
firmware in the tape drive was designed to recognize LEOT (Logical End Of
Tape) and will not access anything beyond that. We have to work with the tape
drive at the firmware level to do what you want, and yes it is expensive
~2-3k for a 4mm.

Also, once you encounter the data beyond the overwrite you are in the middle
of a file within the tar session. We search that data for the signature of
the beginning of the next file, then make a new dummy tape front end that
will syncronize with your data. In other words, tar will be expecting to
encounter the beginning of a file at the point where your first file begins.

Any attempts to recover the data by writing to the tape are clearly
destructive, risky, and not recomended.

Hope I was of some help.

David Corbett
Advanced Data Recovery, Inc.
adr@mind.net

