I don't have experience with the GNU compiler but can give
suggestions for SVR4 and they are probably similar.

Compile the program with the -Kpic option to produce position
independent
code.  Then link it with -dy (to get it dynamically linked) and -G (to 
make it a shared library).

When you compile/link the programs that will use the library you need
to link them
with a -l option.  If you name your library libmine and put it into
/usr/lib then you can use -lmine.  If you put the library somewhere
else you'll also need to use -Lpath to specify the path to your library.
The -L option should precede the -l option on the command line.

-- Doug



