Not exacily, but close.  Newer versions of monitor will give you disk
queue depth[1].

>My suspicion is that the system is terribly I/O-bound, but I need to look at
>wait over time to confirm.  We figured out (over the phone) how to stretch out
>the sample interval, but it still just dumps to the screen.

Let me guess.   He's got a process (or processes) that writes a lot of
data, proably until it exausts all free memory, then all the disks
light up at once[2].  Meanwhile, the user is left waiting on their
prompt to return after typing 'date'.[3].  If the answer to this is
yes, then you are io bound, but it's not your fault...

The best way (that I can think of) to get the answer to your question
is to watch the free page count AND the io numbers.  If there's lots of
io (like the amount of io the drives in question can handle).  



