The C standard says

"Constant expressions shall not contain assignment, increment, decrement
 function-call, or comma operators, except when they are contained within
 the operand of a sizeof operator."

>John
>PS, FWIW, gcc accepts both of these and produces the 'expected' results

By default the language that gcc compiles is not C, it is what is
loosely called "GNU C" which includes a numbver of extensions over
standard C. Use gcc -ansi -pedantic to make gcc an essentially standard C
compiler. If you do you should find that it warns about your code.

