You don't give us much information about which server or which version
of DIGITAL UNIX you have, but my first thought would be that the second
card is not configured into the kernel. You can either boot the generic
kernel and let the system find all the devices, or add the information
by hand to your existing configuration file and rebuild the kernel. On
my AS1000A I have in my configuration file:

                         .
                         .
                         .
controller      tu0        at pci0      slot  11 
controller      tu1        at pci0      slot  12
                         .
                         .
                         .

for the two ethernet cards on the system.
You will also need to run "netconfig" to configure both cards. I suggest
you save your /etc/rc.config at least before doing this.

Regards,
John Hill



