Organization: @Home Network
Reply-To: stufuller@usa.net
NNTP-Posting-Date: Sun, 18 Apr 1999 09:00:04 PDT
Newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1

Chakrapani (kcpani@reliable-net.net) wrote:
: Does anybody know how to configure the second Ethernet board on a
: digital Unix server?  The system is able to recognise the second
: ethernet card at the console level, but Unix is not able to see that as
: a second network device(tu1).  Any clues why?

Go to the kernel config file, /sys/conf/YOUR-HOSTNAME

In that file, you'll find a line of the form

        controller      tu0        at *

or
        controller      tu0        at pci0 slot nn
        
If the first form, just add another line changing "tu0" to "tu1".

If the second form, add another line changing "tu0" to "tu1" and changing the
slot number as needed.

Then,

        # doconfig -c YOUR-HOSTNAME
        
and answer "n" to the prompt.  When the new kernel is built, it'll tell you
where it's at.  Put it into place in your root directory and reboot:

        # mv /vmunix /vmunix.old
        # mv /sys/YOUR-HOSTNAME/vmunix /
        # shutdown -r now
        
After the system reboots, login as root and run /usr/sbin/netsetup

        Stu



