: to skip after the eot mark of the DAT tape and read the
: corrupted tar archive ?

In other words, this user created a tar file on a tape, rewound the tape (due
to using the "rewind" device) and wrote another tar file.

If that's the sequence, then it's likely that you can NOT retrieve the first
tar file.  The DAT drive will record the end of the tape on the tape, and will
not go past it on a read.

There are companies who specialize in retrieving data from situations like
this, but they do it with specialized tape drives and they charge a fortune.  
How bad do you need these files in the lost tar file?  You'll have to need it
pretty bad to justify the cost of this service.

        Stu



