Never seen this but my troubleshooting procedure would run like this.

Assuming 4.0X installed on scsi bus 0 target 6 lun 0 (DKA600 at boot
prompt,
/dev/rrz6c from inside unix)
                3.2X installed on scsi bus 0 target 0 lun 0 (DKA0    at
boot
prompt, /dev/rrz0c from inside unix)


From the console prompt boot DUX4 in single user mode from the generic
console.

>>> boot -fl s -file genvmunix dka600

wait for root prompt

# fsck /dev/rz6a
# mount -u /dev/rz6a /

OK now we have a root filesystem

# mkdir /oldsys
# fsck /dev/rz1a
# mount /dev/rz1a /oldsys

OK now we have both systems mounted

# diff /etc/fstab /oldsys/etc/fstab

