Phil LoCascio wrote:

>     Hi,
>
> using    OSF1 machine.name V4.0 878 alpha , I keep getting segmentation
> faults INSIDE the systems malloc!!
>
> Anyone seen this or know a solution?
>
>     Cheers
>
>     PHiL

Well, thats the normal behaviour if you use more memory then you allocated
using malloc/calloc/realloc.

I.e. you allocated 10 bytes for a string with strlen(string)==10. If you
then do a strcpy(malloced_area, string) it will need 11 bytes!!! 10 bytes
for the string and 1 byte for the final 0-char.

This is the easiest example. In any case the program might or might not
crash depending on how often it uses malloc/calloc/realloc and free.

What you will see is that you get SIGSEGV/SIGBUS in routines like __free
or malloc...

Happy bug hunting,

    Aurel Balmosan.




