In response to Bernhard's question, we have modified the
compiler to allow parameter declarations such as:
    void f(int a[][], int b[][][]);

The first is actually allowed by the Standard.  The second
in non-standard, but gcc accepts it.  Optional messages
can be output for both types.

This change will be available in the Compaq C (formerly DEC C)
compiler in the release after Tru64 UNIX V5.0. The change will
also be available in our Developer's Toolkit compiler, which
is in field test now.

