In sysconfig terms, "dynamic" for *subsystems* means the kernel
module can be unloaded/unconfigured while the machine is up.
"Static" means that the *subsystem* must be linked/unlinked
explicitly when building the kernel; to remove or setup such
a system needs a kernel rebuild/reboot.
But these notions are *different* from the ability to reconfigure
parameters; some parameters can be reconfigured dynamically (while
the machine is up, and taking effect immediately), while some (which
I believe include the shared memory/ipc settings (we've
been through this for Sybase) can be made using sysconfigdb, but will
only take effect on reboot.

Oisin McGuinness


