: Hi everyone,


: I have a DEC Alpha running  Red Haet Linux.
: How can i change to the SRM console to install Digital Unix?
: Any ideas?
What is the exact model of your Alpha box? Some boxes has enough ROM
(Flash) to store both SRM and ARC console. I think you boot your Linux
from ARC console. Try to find the "Change to VMS console" menu in your ARC
menu tree. And do this change. Then you should reboot to get into SRM.
From SRM you can boot the DU install CD issuing:
>>>boot dkaXXX where XXX is yours CD device number (show dev command)
If you want to change back to the ARC console, simple issue:
>>>arc

Hope this help.

Mihaly



