Phil LoCascio wrote:
> 
>     Hi,
> 
> using    OSF1 machine.name V4.0 878 alpha , I keep getting segmentation
> faults INSIDE the systems malloc!!
> 
> Anyone seen this or know a solution?
> 

Well, it _might_ mean there is a bug in malloc, but it's unlikely.

Much more likely is that your application has corrupted the heap. 
Malloc
has control structures in the heap that it uses to keep track of your
allocations; if you write off the 'end' of a block of memory that has
been allocated to you then these structures will be trashed.  

You might find the 'third degree' tool useful - it helps find 
places in your application where you are 'scribbling' on memory
that doesn't belong to you.  Do a 'man third' to learn more about
this tool.

