Hi,

long time ago my company decided to use LSM to handle mirroring. After a lot of
tries, training and workshops, we were able to make a stable and "efficient" LSM
configuration. But we quickly discover that the system we have installed with
LSM are slower than the one without it. We've noticed this in the case where the
server is booting. Some operations can take a lot of time, the loading of huge
database for instance (300 MB) is slower. 
Because LSM is software, you cannot avoid this slowdown.

A customer of mine have had a serious slowdown on his machines running LSM.
Copying very huge files can take a very long time or be interrupted abruptly.
Another disavantage of LSM is his high level of complexity. You cannot avoid to
follow trainings about it. 

If you need a solution to provide resilient disks (mirroring, stripping, ...), I
suggest that you take a look to the Mylex SCSI controller. This is a RAID
controller fully supported by Digital Unix. It take just a few minutes to
configure a mirror set or a RAID-5 set. And because this is a hardware based
solution, you won't see any slowdown of the system ( at human perception of
course).

 
