Homonnai Mihaly wrote:
> 
> I'vea AS1200 with PowerStormD51T and Du4.0D using CDE and OpenGL licence
> and Sw installed on it.
> I'd to use a second monitor as a dual headed  workstation. Is there any
> man page or manual describing how to do this?

I don't remember if that's officially supported on the as1200 so you
are in an experimental area.  If you want to try it....  both cards should
be 51t's with identical texture memory.  Second 51t should have vga
disabled by using the jumper near the card's bulkhead.  Then shutdown
the system, install the card, and reboot.  There *may* be an option
in the /var/X11/Xserver.conf file saying '-onlyScreen0' which, in your
case, should be removed.  Note that the PanoramiX extension isn't
supported by Open3D.  (This extension transparently presents a single
virtual screen built of multiple cards.)

