Homonnai Mihaly wrote:
> 
> I've no there the PS4D51T manual, but as far as i remember, it supports
> 3(1) screens!.

Generally, each particular system is qualified to run a number of heads.
I was mot able to find the info for the as1200 so I am assuming the
most conservative approach.

> It has dual D-sub VGA style connector on the rear side, so
> i think i can connect two monitor  to this bestia.

The light blue connector is video out (VESA standard color 'robins egg blue'
which indicates DDC-capabilities) and the black connector is a vga input
(not supported).  Try 'man ingr' if you have a recent Open3D release.

> It has 16M of VRAm on
> i, and as far as i remember in this configuration this card supports 3
> monitor on 4096x1200 resolition? (may be as a virtual sceer?)
> I'd to use it as a dual headed WS.

This capability is part of PanoramiX (or NT if you use that) and not
supported in Open3D.  A single 51t has a maximum resolution of
1280x1024 pixels, less if stereoscopic display is needed.

